Version drift I hit and corrected against real artifacts rather than memory: Boot 4.1 stopped managing Testcontainers versions, Testcontainers 2.x renamed its modules (testcontainers-postgresql) and dropped the generic on PostgreSQLContainer, Batch 6 moved item APIs to org.springframework.batch.infrastructure.item, and Boot 4 defaults to Jackson 3.

Design decisions worth flagging:

- Fees are not swept as missing payouts. A fee never arrives as its own settlement row — it's deducted in the fee column of its charge's row, and is verified there against the booked FEE ledger entry. Sweeping them would report every ordinary fee as a discrepancy.
- Stripe's CSV reports use major units (120.00) while its API uses minor units. Confirmed from Stripe's docs, not assumed. Conversion uses RoundingMode.UNNECESSARY, so sub-cent precision is a parse failure rather than a silently dropped fraction.
- The live Stripe path renders back into the CSV format and re-enters through the same parser, so pulled data gets the same checksum idempotency and audit storage as an upload, and only one parser is trusted.
- Match rate excludes payout/transfer rows (EXCLUDED) rather than counting them as failures.

